A. Functional requirements

Functional requirements describe what the system should do.

User Registration: Allow new users to create an account.

User Login: Authenticate users using their credentials.

Movie Listing: Display currently available movies.

Movie Details: Show the movie title, language, genre, duration, and description.

Showtime Selection: Allow users to choose a theatre, date, and showtime.

Seat Selection: Display available, selected, and booked seats.

Ticket Booking: Allow users to confirm their bookings.



B. Non-functional requirements

Non-functional requirements describe how well the system should perform.

Performance: Pages and booking details should load quickly under normal usage.

Security: Protect user information and passwords.

Usability: Provide a simple and user-friendly interface.

Reliability: Ensure booking information is stored correctly.

Scalability: Support an increasing number of users and bookings.

Maintainability: Make the code easy to update and maintain.

Data Integrity: Prevent the same seat from being confirmed for two bookings in the same show.

